{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e50c06bdbcfd0dcb","type":"group","x":-1099,"y":-250,"width":1355,"height":1450,"label":"Flow with Learning Processes"},
		{"id":"281cc8f3d0296d61","type":"group","x":341,"y":-37,"width":759,"height":1237,"label":"Principles for Efficiency"},
		{"id":"1e54314c10a5c851","type":"text","text":"# Attention Gateway","x":-1079,"y":-230,"width":320,"height":50},
		{"id":"f04a658e9d78cdd0","type":"text","text":"# Encoding Gateway","x":-659,"y":-230,"width":320,"height":50},
		{"id":"72e0672cae02e0c3","type":"text","text":"# Focus","x":-1044,"y":-17,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4a0df928ace34a00","type":"text","text":"# FER-MO","x":-409,"y":-450,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9c3e6cd917b8092f","type":"text","text":"# Storage via Retrieval Gateway","x":-284,"y":-230,"width":520,"height":50},
		{"id":"a0034f89b860a9a3","type":"text","text":"### External\n- Remove Environmental Distractions\n- Clean up clutter and workspace.","x":-1044,"y":74,"width":250,"height":193},
		{"id":"21481644c49f2187","type":"text","text":"### During Learning (Within a Topic)\n\n- Read for 1-2 minutes\n- Perform Metacognition in the process.\n- Recall new content onto mind map.","x":-147,"y":172,"width":250,"height":318},
		{"id":"cbf821b115ca7d80","type":"text","text":"# Retrieval","x":-147,"y":-17,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ba55df835a3e9823","type":"text","text":"# Encoding","x":-625,"y":-17,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2cae45594705c2bd","type":"text","text":"### Metacognition - G.R.I.N.D.E (Justin Sung)\n- Keep in mind:\n\t- Grouping\n\t- Relationships\n\t- Interconnected\n\t- Non-Verbal\n\t- Directional\n\t- Emphasized\n- Keys for good mind-mapping and encoding.","x":-624,"y":760,"width":250,"height":380},
		{"id":"f0a2d8ec888cf0a4","type":"text","text":"# Metacognition","x":407,"y":-17,"width":267,"height":60},
		{"id":"34497cdbe54d9d25","type":"text","text":"### Internal\n- Pray\n- 5 Deep Breaths\n- Clear the mind","x":-1044,"y":300,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"5a71f84abb77ecca","type":"text","text":"### Preliminary\n- Skim over proceeding topics.\n- Ask questions, create hypothesis, and make predictions.\n- Get a \"lay of the land.\"","x":-1044,"y":493,"width":250,"height":247},
		{"id":"8b59b5c4cfbceb7f","type":"text","text":"### Mind mapping\n- Design to force the brain into building relationships and connections.","x":-625,"y":172,"width":250,"height":191},
		{"id":"375a6015bde15aad","type":"text","text":"### Foundation\n- Before diving in:\n\t- Write down questions.\n\t- Hypothesis\n\t- Initial structure of keywords and terms.","x":-625,"y":420,"width":250,"height":286},
		{"id":"9d244a5ee2b14c5e","type":"text","text":"### G.R.I.N.D.E (Justin Sung)\n\n- Think about\n\t- Grouping\n\t- Relationships\n\t- Interconnected\n\t- Non-Verbal\n\t- Directional\n\t- Emphasized\n- Do this while **encoding**.\n\nIncreases cognitive load, promote proper encoding, creates more direction for a better mind map.\n\n","x":416,"y":74,"width":250,"height":465},
		{"id":"eec732ccdd0749e0","type":"text","text":"### After a Topic\n- Grab a new sheet of paper.\n- Rebuild mind map from memory\n- DOESN'T HAVE TO BE ACCURATE.\n- Organize content and relationships in a better SCHEMA.","x":-147,"y":539,"width":250,"height":334},
		{"id":"51956fbb2215b905","type":"text","text":"### General Metacognition\n\n- Ask questions\n- Formulate synthesis.\n- Make predictions.\n- Do this while **conducting preliminary** and **encoding**.","x":416,"y":585,"width":250,"height":288},
		{"id":"bc6c706b45155db4","type":"text","text":"# Organization","x":796,"y":-17,"width":246,"height":60},
		{"id":"283c1376085845fc","type":"text","text":"### Time Management\n- Work in blocks of 45 minutes.\n- Take 10 minute breaks.\n- Avoid doom scrolling or anything **dopamine heavy** during breaks.","x":793,"y":101,"width":250,"height":319},
		{"id":"54f6dabd64ffe7fb","x":796,"y":585,"width":250,"height":319,"type":"text","text":"### Recommendations (Justin Sung)\n\n- Mind mapping is a skill.\n- Skill takes progress.\n- Focus on building each step of the process **one at a time**."}
	],
